    "review_decision": "counterexample_found_substrate_owned_mcm_atpase_analog_sites_not_cdc7_transfer",
    "source_basis": "RCSB title and primary citation identify a Cdc7-Dbf4 kinase-dependent MCM2-7 phosphorylation complex, but the local BEF/ADP groups that produce within-6-Angstrom contacts are associated with MCM3/MCM4/MCM5/MCM7 helicase ATPase chains. The only Cdc7-associated BEF record is nearest to DBF4 Tyr668 at 13.833 Angstrom and has no local MCM phosphoacceptor candidate.",
    "source_limitations": [
      "Reject local MCM-chain BEF-to-MCM Ser/Thr contacts as ePK positive evidence because the donor analog belongs to MCM helicase ATPase sites, not the Cdc7 kinase active site.",
      "This is a source-mapped counterexample for transition-analog searches inside large kinase-substrate assemblies."
    ],
